Description: Convert an effect preview's format before its sink
 The effects grid joins each preview, "... ! FILTER name=last", to
 glupload ! qml6glsink with nothing that converts after the filter. The
 effectv elements (dicetv, edgetv, agingtv, optv, quarktv, radioactv,
 revtv, rippletv, shagadelictv, streaktv, vertigotv, warptv) give only
 RGBx, xRGB, BGRx and xBGR, and qml6glsink takes RGBA, BGRA, RGB, YV12 and
 NV12 as GL memory, so their previews stop ("reason not-linked"); in 2D
 the grid then removes those twelve rows, in 3D they stay black. One
 videoconvert now stands between the filter and the upload, as one
 already stands before the filter (linkEffectPreview() in
 src/video/effectpreview.h). The camera's own pipeline was not affected:
 camerabin's viewfinder bin converts by itself. The test joins every
 filter of Config.qml's model through that function to qml6glsink's own
 template in system memory; without the conversion the twelve fail.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24

